marshmallow-rust attribution and scope
=======================================

This project is a standalone Rust port of the `marshmallow`
object-serialization/validation library. It is MIT licensed (see LICENSE);
it vendors no upstream code.

Behavior, field semantics, error-message texts, and the `Schema`
dump/load/validate entry-point shapes are modelled on:

  marshmallow-code/marshmallow — https://github.com/marshmallow-code/marshmallow
  Copyright Steven Loria and contributors; MIT License
  (see https://github.com/marshmallow-code/marshmallow/blob/dev/LICENSE).

Ported against marshmallow 4.3.1. The `marshmallow` package itself is a
runtime dependency (it provides the `Schema` base class, the field and
validator classes the compiler inspects, and the pure-Python fallback
path); it is not vendored here.

`tests/corpus/*` are original fixtures written for this port (not copied
from the marshmallow test suite). The equivalence harness
(`tests/equiv.py`) and the upstream-suite gate compare against the
installed `marshmallow` package only at test time.
